(BUF-30: undocumented precision on OOB - a READ is bounds-checked against current SIZE, not capacity, so an index within capacity but past current size still errors.)
(expected output:
read past size (but within capacity) errored
0
)
a buffer called fx is 8 bytes in size.
append "ABCD" to fx.
Set byte 6 of fx to 88.
a number called atcap is byte 8 of fx.
On error print "read past size (but within capacity) errored".
print atcap.
